BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the physical mechanisms governing the Enhanced Greenhouse Effect, detailing infrared absorption bands of greenhouse gases and Radiative Forcing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Physical Mechanics of the Greenhouse Effect, Molecular Spectroscopy, and Radiative Forcing:) Tj
T*
(   1. Planetary Energy Balance:) Tj
T*
(   - Solar Radiation \(Shortwave\): The sun emits shortwave blackbody radiation \(effective) Tj
T*
(   temperature ~5,800 K\) with spectral irradiance peaking in the visible and near-ultraviolet) Tj
T*
(   range \(0.2 to 2.0 micrometers\). The solar constant at the top of Earth's atmosphere is S_0 ~) Tj
T*
(   1,361 W/m2. Accounting for planetary albedo \(alpha ~ 0.30\) and spherical surface geometry,) Tj
T*
(   Earth absorbs:) Tj
T*
(   F_in = S_0 * \(1 - alpha\) / 4 = 1,361 * \(1 - 0.30\) / 4 ~ 238 W/m2.) Tj
T*
(   - Terrestrial Radiation \(Longwave Infrared\): In thermal steady state, Earth re-radiates this) Tj
T*
(   absorbed energy back into space as longwave infrared \(LWIR\) radiation \(temperature ~255 K,) Tj
T*
(   peaking at 8 to 15 micrometers\).) Tj
T*
(   - Without an atmosphere, Earth's radiative equilibrium surface temperature would be:) Tj
T*
(   T_e = [ F_in / sigma ]^\(1/4\) = [ 238 / \(5.67 * 10^-8\) ]^\(1/4\) ~ 255 K \(-18 deg C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Natural Greenhouse Effect: Atmospheric greenhouse gases absorb outgoing infrared photons and) Tj
T*
(   re-radiate thermal energy isotropically \(both upward to space and downward to the surface\),) Tj
T*
(   elevating mean global surface temperature to +15 deg C \(288 K\), a 33 deg C natural warming.) Tj
T*
(   2. Molecular Vibrational Infrared Absorption:) Tj
T*
(   - For a molecule to absorb infrared photons, its vibrational mode must induce a transient) Tj
T*
(   change in its molecular dipole moment:) Tj
T*
(   - Diatomic symmetric gases \(N2, O2, 99% of atmosphere\) cannot acquire a dynamic dipole moment) Tj
T*
(   during vibration, rendering them transparent to infrared.) Tj
T*
(   - Polyatomic Greenhouse Gases:) Tj
T*
(   * Carbon Dioxide \(CO2\): A linear molecule. The symmetric stretch is IR-inactive, but the) Tj
T*
(   degenerate Bending Mode \(nu_2\) at 667 cm^-1 \(wavelength 15.0 micrometers\) and asymmetric) Tj
T*
(   stretch \(nu_3, 4.3 micrometers\) induce powerful oscillating dipoles, strongly absorbing IR) Tj
T*
(   precisely near the peak of Earth's terrestrial emission spectrum.) Tj
T*
(   * Methane \(CH4\): Tetrahedral geometry. Bending and stretching modes at 7.7 and 3.3 micrometers) Tj
T*
(   absorb within the 'atmospheric window' \(7 to 13 micrometers\) where CO2 absorption is weak.) Tj
T*
(   3. Enhanced Radiative Forcing \(Delta F\):) Tj
T*
(   - Defined as the net change in downward radiative flux \(W/m2\) at the tropopause caused by an) Tj
T*
(   external perturbation:) Tj
T*
(   Delta F = 5.35 * ln\( C / C_0 \)) Tj
T*
(   - The logarithmic dependence reflects spectroscopic saturation: the central 15-micrometer CO2) Tj
T*
(   band is nearly saturated, and additional warming occurs primarily by broadening the band wings.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
