(   [Problem Statement]: Define Global Warming Potential \(GWP\) and Atmospheric Lifetime, and compare the radiative efficiencies of CO2, CH4, N2O, and SF6.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Global Warming Potential \(GWP\), Radiative Efficiency, and Greenhouse Gas Metrics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Mathematical Formulation of GWP:) Tj
T*
(   Established by the IPCC, the Global Warming Potential \(GWP\) measures the time-integrated) Tj
T*
(   radiative forcing of a pulse emission of 1 kg of a specific greenhouse gas \(x\) relative to 1 kg) Tj
T*
(   of reference carbon dioxide \(CO2\) over a defined time horizon \(TH, typically 20 or 100 years\):) Tj
T*
(   GWP_x\(TH\) = [ Integral_{0}^{TH} a_x * C_x\(t\) dt ] / [ Integral_{0}^{TH} a_{CO2} * C_{CO2}\(t\) dt) Tj
T*
(   ]) Tj
T*
(   Where:) Tj
T*
