(   - a_x: Radiative efficiency of gas x \(W/m2 per kg of atmospheric concentration increase\).) Tj
T*
(   - C_x\(t\): Atmospheric mass of gas x remaining at time t following a pulse emission.) Tj
T*
(   - a_{CO2} and C_{CO2}\(t\): Corresponding parameters for reference gas CO2.) Tj
T*
(   2. Atmospheric Lifetimes and Removal Kinetics:) Tj
T*
(   - Methane \(CH4\): Atmospheric lifetime ~11.8 years. Removed primarily by tropospheric gas-phase) Tj
T*
(   oxidation via hydroxyl radicals \(.OH\):) Tj
T*
(   CH4 + .OH -> .CH3 + H2O.) Tj
T*
(   - Nitrous Oxide \(N2O\): Atmospheric lifetime ~109 years. Unreactive in the troposphere;) Tj
T*
(   destroyed in the stratosphere by photolysis and reaction with excited oxygen atoms [O\(.1D\)].) Tj
T*
(   - Sulfur Hexafluoride \(SF6\): Atmospheric lifetime ~3,200 years. Highly inert octahedron;) Tj
T*
(   destroyed only by high-energy photolysis in the mesosphere.) Tj
T*
(   - Carbon Dioxide \(CO2\): Lacks a single simple first-order decay lifetime! It is governed by a) Tj
T*
(   sum of multi-timescale carbon cycle sinks \(ocean mixed layer uptake: decades; deep oceanic) Tj
T*
(   circulation: centuries; mineral silicate weathering: tens of millennia\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Comparative Matrix \(IPCC AR6 Metrics over 100-Year Horizon\):) Tj
T*
(   - Carbon Dioxide \(CO2\): Lifetime = Variable \(multi-millennial\); Radiative Efficiency = 1.37 *) Tj
T*
(   10^-5 W/m2/ppb; GWP100 = 1.0 \(Baseline\).) Tj
T*
(   - Methane \(CH4\): Lifetime = 11.8 years; Radiative Efficiency = 3.88 * 10^-4 W/m2/ppb; GWP100 =) Tj
T*
(   27.9 \(approx 28\) \(and GWP20 = 84 over 20-year horizon\).) Tj
T*
(   - Nitrous Oxide \(N2O\): Lifetime = 109 years; Radiative Efficiency = 3.00 * 10^-3 W/m2/ppb;) Tj
T*
(   GWP100 = 273.) Tj
T*
(   - Sulfur Hexafluoride \(SF6\): Lifetime = 3,200 years; Radiative Efficiency = 0.57 W/m2/ppb;) Tj
T*
(   GWP100 = 23,500.) Tj
T*
