(   calcification escalates, resulting in thinned shells and skeletal dissolution.) Tj
T*
(   4. Molecular Mechanism of Thermal Coral Bleaching:) Tj
T*
(   - Scleractinian corals maintain an obligate mutualistic endosymbiosis with photosynthetic) Tj
T*
(   dinoflagellates \(zooxanthellae, Symbiodiniaceae\) living within their gastrodermal cells.) Tj
T*
(   - Elevated Sea Surface Temperature \(SST > 1 to 2 deg C above summer maximum\): Causes thermal) Tj
T*
(   damage to zooxanthellae Photosystem II \(D1 protein denaturation\).) Tj
T*
(   - Photoinhibition triggers excessive production of toxic Reactive Oxygen Species \(ROS, .O2-,) Tj
T*
(   H2O2, .OH\) within algal chloroplasts, which leak into coral host cells.) Tj
T*
(   - To prevent oxidative necrosis, the coral animal host expels its zooxanthellae symbionts. The) Tj
T*
(   coral tissue becomes transparent, revealing the white calcium carbonate skeleton underneath) Tj
T*
(   \('bleached'\). Lacking algal photosynthetic glucose, corals starve and suffer mass mortality) Tj
T*
(   within weeks.) Tj
