(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the Chapman Photochemical Mechanism of stratospheric ozone, and derive the catalytic ozone destruction cycles by halogen radicals.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Chapman Photochemical Mechanism and Catalytic Ozone Destruction Kinetics:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Classical Chapman Mechanism \(Sydney Chapman, 1930\):) Tj
T*
(   Describes the natural, non-catalytic steady-state formation and destruction of ozone in the) Tj
T*
(   pristine stratosphere:) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 1 \(Photolytic Initiation\): Molecular oxygen absorbs high-energy shortwave solar UV-C) Tj
T*
(   \(lambda < 242 nm\), splitting into two ground-state oxygen atoms:) Tj
T*
(   O2 + h*nu \(lambda < 242 nm\) -> 2 O\(.3P\)) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 2 \(Ozone Synthesis\): Atomic oxygen rapidly combines with O2 in the presence of an) Tj
T*
(   inert third-body molecule \(M = N2 or O2\) that absorbs excess kinetic energy:) Tj
T*
(   O\(.3P\) + O2 + M -> O3 + M \(k2 = 6.0 * 10^-34 cm6/molecule2/s\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 3 \(Ozone Photolysis\): Ozone absorbs UV-B and UV-C solar photons \(lambda = 200 to 310) Tj
T*
(   nm, Hartley band\), dissociating:) Tj
T*
(   O3 + h*nu -> O2 + O\(.1D\) \(Reversible odd-oxygen interconversion\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction 4 \(Natural Radical Termination\): Ozone reacts with atomic oxygen to form two) Tj
T*
(   molecular oxygen molecules:) Tj
T*
(   O3 + O\(.3P\) -> 2 O2 \(k4 = 8.0 * 10^-15 cm3/molecule/s, slow reaction\).) Tj
T*
(   At steady state, the Chapman cycle predicts stratospheric ozone concentrations roughly double) Tj
T*
(   those observed empirically, proving that additional catalytic destruction pathways must) Tj
T*
(   operate.) Tj
T*
(   2. Homogeneous Catalytic Destruction Cycles \(Paul Crutzen, Mario Molina, Sherwood Rowland\):) Tj
T*
(   Trace radical catalysts \(X. = .OH, .NO, .Cl, .Br\) destroy ozone through a cyclic chain reaction) Tj
T*
(   without being consumed:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: X. + O3 -> XO. + O2) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: XO. + O -> X. + O2) Tj
T*
(   - Net Reaction: O3 + O -> 2 O2) Tj
T*
(   The catalyst X. is regenerated in Step 2, ready to destroy another ozone molecule.) Tj
T*
(   3. Halogen Catalysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Chlorofluorocarbons \(e.g., CFC-11 CFCl3, CFC-12 CF2Cl2\) are chemically inert in the) Tj
T*
(   troposphere. They ascend into the mid-stratosphere \(25 to 35 km altitude\), where shortwave UV) Tj
T*
(   radiation photolyzes C-Cl bonds:) Tj
T*
(   CF2Cl2 + h*nu \(lambda < 220 nm\) -> .CF2Cl + Cl.) Tj
T*
(   - The released atomic chlorine radical \(Cl.\) drives the catalytic cycle:) Tj
T*
(   Cl. + O3 -> ClO. + O2) Tj
T*
(   ClO. + O -> Cl. + O2) Tj
T*
(   - A single chlorine radical cycles through this loop up to 100,000 times before being) Tj
T*
(   temporarily sequestered into stable reservoir species \(HCl and ClONO2\).) Tj
T*
ET

