(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the Montreal Protocol \(1987\) and Kigali Amendment \(2016\), explaining Ozone Depletion Potential \(ODP\) and HFC phase-down.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Montreal Protocol, Kigali Amendment, and Atmospheric Governance:) Tj
T*
(   1. Historical Genesis and Institutional Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Adopted in September 1987 under the Vienna Convention for the Protection of the Ozone Layer,) Tj
T*
(   the Montreal Protocol is universally recognized as the most successful multilateral) Tj
T*
(   environmental agreement in history, ratified by all 198 UN member states.) Tj
T*
(   2. Ozone Depletion Potential \(ODP\):) Tj
T*
(   ODP is the ratio of the calculated steady-state ozone destruction per unit mass of a compound) Tj
T*
(   relative to the reference compound Trichlorofluoromethane \(CFC-11, assigned ODP = 1.0\):) Tj
T*
(   - CFC-11 \(CFCl3\): ODP = 1.0.) Tj
T*
(   - CFC-12 \(CF2Cl2\): ODP = 1.0.) Tj
T*
(   - Halon-1301 \(CF3Br\): ODP = 10.0 \(Atomic bromine is ~40-60 times more destructive per atom than) Tj
T*
(   chlorine due to weaker bonding with reservoirs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hydrochlorofluorocarbons \(HCFC-22, CHClF2\): ODP = 0.055 \(Tropospheric C-H bonds allow 90% OH) Tj
T*
(   oxidation before reaching the stratosphere; used as transitional substitutes\).) Tj
T*
(   3. The Technological Transition and The HFC Dilemma:) Tj
T*
(   - The protocol successfully phased out production and consumption of CFCs \(by 1996 in developed) Tj
T*
(   nations; by 2010 in developing nations\) and HCFCs \(scheduled for complete phase-out by 2030\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hydrofluorocarbons \(HFCs, e.g., HFC-134a, CH2FCF3\) were developed as permanent) Tj
T*
(   non-ozone-depleting replacements \(ODP = 0 because they contain zero chlorine or bromine atoms\).) Tj
T*
(   - The Unintended Climate Impact: While HFCs do not destroy stratospheric ozone, they are) Tj
T*
(   super-greenhouse gases with Global Warming Potentials thousands of times greater than CO2!) Tj
T*
(   Rapidly growing HFC use in commercial air conditioning threatened to add 0.5 deg C of global) Tj
T*
(   warming by 2100.) Tj
T*
(   4. The Kigali Amendment \(2016\):) Tj
T*
(   - Adopted in October 2016 in Kigali, Rwanda, amending the Montreal Protocol to legally mandate) Tj
T*
(   the phase-down of production and consumption of 18 specific HFCs by 80-85% by the late 2040s.) Tj
T*
(   - Stratified Timetables: Developed nations began phase-down in 2019; developing nations \(Group) Tj
T*
(   1: China, Brazil\) freeze in 2024; high-ambient temperature nations \(Group 2: India, Gulf) Tj
T*
(   states\) freeze in 2028.) Tj
T*
(   - Climate Benefit: Prevents up to 105 million metric tons of CO2 equivalent emissions by 2100,) Tj
T*
(   avoiding up to 0.44 deg C of global temperature rise, while transitioning cooling technologies) Tj
T*
(   to natural low-GWP refrigerants \(hydrocarbons: R290 propane, R600a isobutane;) Tj
T*
(   hydrofluoroolefins: HFOs\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
