(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the legal and policy framework of the 2015 Paris Agreement, detailing Nationally Determined Contributions \(NDCs\) and Article 6 market mechanisms.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The 2015 Paris Agreement: Dynamic Architecture, NDCs, and Article 6 Governance:) Tj
T*
(   1. Foundational Paradigm Shift:) Tj
T*
(   Adopted at COP-21 in December 2015, the Paris Agreement replaced the rigid top-down annex) Tj
T*
(   bifurcation of the Kyoto Protocol with an inclusive, dynamic hybrid architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Long-Term Temperature Goal \(Article 2.1\(a\)\): Holding the increase in global average surface) Tj
T*
(   temperature to 'well below 2.0 deg C above pre-industrial levels and pursuing efforts to limit) Tj
T*
(   the temperature increase to 1.5 deg C.') Tj
T*
(   - Global Peaking and Net-Zero Balance \(Article 4.1\): Achieving a global peak of GHG emissions) Tj
T*
(   as soon as possible and achieving a balance between anthropogenic emissions by sources and) Tj
T*
(   removals by sinks \(Net-Zero greenhouse gas emissions\) in the second half of this century.) Tj
T*
(   2. Nationally Determined Contributions \(NDCs, Article 4\):) Tj
T*
(   - Bottom-Up Pledges: Every state party \(both developed and developing\) is legally obligated to) Tj
T*
(   prepare, communicate, and maintain successive national climate mitigation pledges.) Tj
T*
(   - The Principle of Progression and Non-Regression \(The Ratchet Mechanism\):) Tj
T*
(   Each successive NDC submitted every five years must represent a progression beyond the party's) Tj
T*
(   previous NDC and reflect its highest possible ambition.) Tj
T*
(   - Global Stocktake \(Article 14\): A comprehensive collective assessment conducted every five) Tj
T*
(   years \(first concluded in 2023 at COP-28\) evaluating aggregate global progress toward the 1.5) Tj
T*
(   deg C goal.) Tj
T*
(   3. Article 6 Market and Non-Market Mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   Establishes international cooperation for transferring mitigation outcomes:) Tj
T*
(   - Article 6.2 \(Bilateral Cooperative Approaches\):) Tj
T*
(   Authorizes two state parties to bilaterally trade Internationally Transferred Mitigation) Tj
T*
(   Outcomes \(ITMOs\). Mandates rigorous Corresponding Adjustments to prevent 'double-counting' of) Tj
T*
(   the same emission reduction by both the buyer and seller nations.) Tj
T*
