(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the statutory regulatory architecture of the Water \(Prevention and Control of Pollution\) Act 1974, detailing Consent to Establish \(CTE\) and SPCB powers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Water \(Prevention and Control of Pollution\) Act, 1974: Regulatory Mechanisms and Statutory) Tj
T*
(   Powers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Legislative Genesis and Constitutional Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   Enacted under Article 252\(1\) of the Constitution pursuant to resolutions passed by state) Tj
T*
(   legislatures, the Water Act represents India's pioneering comprehensive pollution control) Tj
T*
(   statute, establishing specialized institutional bodies: the Central Pollution Control Board) Tj
T*
(   \(CPCB\) and State Pollution Control Boards \(SPCBs\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Functions of Pollution Control Boards:) Tj
T*
(   - Central Pollution Control Board \(CPCB, Section 16\): Coordinates state board activities,) Tj
T*
(   provides technical assistance, establishes comprehensive national water quality standards, and) Tj
T*
(   advises the Central Government.) Tj
T*
(   - State Pollution Control Boards \(SPCBs, Section 17\): Inspects industrial wastewater treatment) Tj
