(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the provisions of the Air \(Prevention and Control of Pollution\) Act 1981, including Air Pollution Control Areas and emission standards.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Air \(Prevention and Control of Pollution\) Act, 1981: Regulatory Framework and Enforcement:) Tj
T*
(   1. Constitutional Authority and Statutory Genesis:) Tj
T*
(   Enacted under Article 253 of the Constitution to implement the international decisions taken at) Tj
T*
(   the United Nations Conference on the Human Environment held at Stockholm in June 1972. The Act) Tj
T*
(   applies the existing CPCB and SPCB institutional machinery established under the Water Act to) Tj
T*
(   combat atmospheric contamination.) Tj
T*
(   2. Statutory Declaration of Air Pollution Control Areas \(Section 19\):) Tj
T*
(   - The State Government, after consultation with the SPCB, is empowered by official gazette) Tj
T*
(   notification to declare any geographic area or areas within the state as an 'Air Pollution) Tj
T*
(   Control Area.') Tj
T*
(   - In practice, state governments have declared the ENTIRE geographical territory of states as) Tj
T*
(   Air Pollution Control Areas to ensure universal compliance.) Tj
T*
(   - Power to Prohibit Specific Fuels and Appliances: In declared control areas, the State) Tj
T*
(   Government can prohibit the use of specific high-polluting fuels \(e.g., petcoke, furnace oil,) Tj
T*
(   unwashed high-sulfur coal\) and prohibit the burning of agricultural residues or waste) Tj
T*
(   materials.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Consent Regime for Air-Polluting Industries \(Section 21\):) Tj
T*
(   - No person can operate any industrial plant in an air pollution control area without obtaining) Tj
T*
(   prior written consent from the SPCB.) Tj
T*
(   - Consent Conditions: Mandatory installation of approved air pollution control equipment) Tj
T*
