(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the regulatory mechanisms of the Forest \(Conservation\) Act, 1980, restrictions on forest diversion, and Compensatory Afforestation \(CAMPA\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Forest \(Conservation\) Act, 1980, Non-Forest Diversion, and the CAMPA Regulatory) Tj
T*
(   Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   1. Historical Impetus:) Tj
T*
(   Prior to 1976, 'Forests' was an exclusive State legislative subject under the Constitution.) Tj
T*
(   Between 1951 and 1980, state governments indiscriminately diverted over 4.3 million hectares of) Tj
T*
(   pristine forest land \(averaging ~150,000 ha/year\) for agriculture, dams, and industrial) Tj
T*
(   colonization.) Tj
T*
(   - 42nd Amendment \(1976\): Transferred 'Forests' to the Concurrent List \(Entry 17A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Enactment of FCA 1980: Halted unilateral state forest clearing by centralizing forest) Tj
T*
(   diversion approval.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mandatory Central Approval \(Section 2\):) Tj
T*
(   Section 2 mandates that 'Notwithstanding anything contained in any other law for the time being) Tj
T*
(   in force in a State, no State Government or other authority shall make, except with the prior) Tj
T*
(   approval of the Central Government, any order directing:) Tj
T*
(   - \(i\) That any reserved forest shall cease to be reserved.) Tj
T*
(   - \(ii\) That any forest land or any portion thereof may be used for any non-forest purpose.) Tj
T*
(   - \(iii\) That any forest land may be assigned by way of lease to any private person or) Tj
T*
(   non-governmental corporation.) Tj
T*
(   - \(iv\) That any forest land may be cleared of trees which have grown naturally in that land.') Tj
T*
(   - Impact: Annual forest diversion dropped from 150,000 ha/year to under 25,000 ha/year.) Tj
T*
(   3. Compensatory Afforestation and CAMPA:) Tj
T*
(   Whenever forest land is approved for diversion for industrial or infrastructure purposes) Tj
T*
(   \(mining, dams, highways\), the project proponent must fulfill two mandatory statutory financial) Tj
T*
(   compensations:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Compensatory Afforestation \(CA\):) Tj
T*
(   * The user agency must provide non-forest land of equivalent area adjacent to a protected) Tj
T*
(   forest, or degraded forest land of double the area, and deposit the full financial cost of) Tj
T*
(   planting and maintaining native trees for 10 years.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Net Present Value \(NPV\):) Tj
T*
(   * Formulated by the Supreme Court in the landmark T.N. Godavarman Thirumulpad case: The) Tj
T*
(   economic value of ecosystem services \(carbon sequestration, water recharge, biodiversity\) lost) Tj
T*
(   due to forest diversion over a 50-year period must be compensated financially.) Tj
T*
(   * The user agency must pay the statutory NPV \(ranging from 10 lakh to 16 lakh rupees per) Tj
T*
(   hectare, depending on canopy density and forest eco-class\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compensatory Afforestation Fund Management and Planning Authority \(CAMPA\):) Tj
T*
(   Codified under the Compensatory Afforestation Fund Act, 2016, managing over 50,000 crore rupees) Tj
T*
(   in National and State funds dedicated exclusively to artificial regeneration, assisted natural) Tj
T*
(   regeneration, wildlife habitat enrichment, and forest fire control.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
