(   1. Statutory Genesis and International Standing:) Tj
T*
(   Established on October 18, 2010, under the National Green Tribunal Act 2010 pursuant to Article) Tj
T*
(   21 constitutional jurisprudence, India became only the third nation in the world \(after) Tj
T*
(   Australia and New Zealand\) to establish a specialized environmental tribunal.) Tj
T*
(   2. Specialized Composition:) Tj
T*
(   - Unique Multi-Disciplinary Bench: Every NGT bench comprises an equal balance of:) Tj
T*
(   * Judicial Members: Retired judges of the Supreme Court or Chief Justices of High Courts) Tj
T*
(   \(headed by the Chairperson in Principal Bench, New Delhi\).) Tj
T*
(   * Expert Members: Highly qualified scientists and technical experts holding doctorates in) Tj
T*
(   environmental engineering, ecology, or forestry with over 15 years of practical field) Tj
T*
(   experience.) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates judicial dependence on outside expert witnesses, ensuring fast, scientifically) Tj
T*
(   robust adjudication.) Tj
T*
(   3. Statutory Jurisdiction \(Section 14, 15, and 16\):) Tj
T*
(   - Original Jurisdiction \(Section 14\): Over all civil cases where a substantial question) Tj
T*
(   relating to the environment \(including environmental damage and public health\) is involved,) Tj
T*
(   arising out of the implementation of seven specified environmental statutes:) Tj
T*
(   * 1. Water Act, 1974) Tj
T*
(   * 2. Water Cess Act, 1977) Tj
T*
(   * 3. Forest \(Conservation\) Act, 1980) Tj
T*
(   * 4. Air Act, 1981) Tj
T*
(   * 5. Environment \(Protection\) Act, 1986) Tj
T*
(   * 6. Public Liability Insurance Act, 1991) Tj
T*
(   * 7. Biological Diversity Act, 2002) Tj
T*
(   \(Note: Wildlife Protection Act 1972 and Indian Forest Act 1927 are explicitly excluded from NGT) Tj
T*
(   jurisdiction\).) Tj
T*
(   - Relief and Compensation \(Section 15\): Directing restitution of damaged ecosystems, relief to) Tj
T*
(   pollution victims, and clean-up costs.) Tj
T*
(   - Appellate Jurisdiction \(Section 16\): Hearing statutory appeals challenging Environmental) Tj
T*
(   Clearances \(EC\) or CTO rejections within 30 days.) Tj
T*
(   4. Landmark NGT Precedents:) Tj
T*
(   - Ban on 10-Year-Old Diesel Vehicles in Delhi-NCR \(Vardhaman Kaushik case\): Prohibited older) Tj
T*
(   diesel vehicles to curb toxic PM2.5 air pollution.) Tj
T*
(   - Ban on Rat-Hole Coal Mining in Meghalaya: Halted hazardous unscientific coal mining causing) Tj
T*
(   severe acid mine drainage that turned the Kopili and Lukha rivers toxic.) Tj
T*
(   - Art of Living Yamuna Floodplain Fine: Imposed environmental restoration restitution fees of 5) Tj
T*
(   crore rupees for damaging sensitive riparian floodplains during the World Culture Festival.) Tj
T*
