12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the four sequential stages of Environmental Impact Assessment \(EIA\) under the EIA Notification 2006: Screening, Scoping, Public Consultation, and Appraisal.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Four Sequential Stages of Environmental Impact Assessment \(EIA Notification 2006\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Regulatory Mandate:) Tj
T*
(   Issued under the Environment \(Protection\) Act, 1986, the EIA Notification 2006 mandates that) Tj
T*
(   prior environmental clearance \(EC\) must be obtained before initiating construction or expansion) Tj
T*
(   of specified developmental projects listed in the Schedule.) Tj
T*
(   2. Category A vs. Category B Project Classification:) Tj
T*
(   - Category A: High-impact projects \(e.g., nuclear power, ports, large chemical refineries,) Tj
T*
(   thermal power plants >= 500 MW, mining leases > 100 ha\). Processed at the central level by the) Tj
T*
(   Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change \(MoEFCC\) upon the recommendation of the) Tj
T*
(   Central Expert Appraisal Committee \(EAC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Category B: Moderate-impact projects. Processed at the state level by the State Environment) Tj
T*
