BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the procedure, legal significance, and statutory exemptions of the Public Consultation process under the EIA Notification 2006.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Public Consultation in Indian EIA: Legal Architecture, Hearing Procedure, and Statutory) Tj
T*
(   Exemptions:) Tj
T*
(   1. Democratic and Environmental Justice Foundation:) Tj
T*
(   Public Consultation is the statutory mechanism through which the concerns of local affected) Tj
T*
(   persons, tribal inhabitants, and civil society regarding the environmental consequences of a) Tj
T*
(   proposed industrial project are formally elicited, recorded, and addressed. It embodies) Tj
T*
(   participatory environmental democracy and the Right to Information.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Two Limbs of Public Consultation:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Public Hearing at the Site:) Tj
T*
(   * Conducted in the immediate vicinity of the proposed project site or at the district) Tj
T*
(   headquarters.) Tj
T*
(   * Presided over by the District Magistrate \(Collector / Deputy Commissioner\) or an officer not) Tj
T*
(   below the rank of Additional District Magistrate, assisted by a representative of the State) Tj
T*
(   Pollution Control Board \(SPCB\).) Tj
T*
(   * Notice Period: A minimum notice period of 30 days must be provided to the public via) Tj
T*
(   advertisements in at least one national daily newspaper and one regional language newspaper.) Tj
T*
(   * Video-Recording: The entire proceeding must be continuously video-recorded, and the minutes) Tj
T*
(   must be signed on-site by the District Magistrate and published on the SPCB website.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Written Responses from Other Concerned Persons:) Tj
T*
(   * Any person, NGO, or institution can submit written representations, comments, and objections) Tj
T*
(   directly to the SPCB or regulatory authority.) Tj
T*
(   3. Integration into Final EIA:) Tj
T*
(   The project proponent must address every material concern raised during the public hearing,) Tj
T*
(   modify the Environmental Management Plan \(EMP\) accordingly, and submit a detailed action plan) Tj
T*
(   with cost allocations.) Tj
T*
