(   Thrust \(HFT\), Main Boundary Thrust \(MBT\), and Main Central Thrust \(MCT\), making the Indian) Tj
T*
(   subcontinent highly seismically vulnerable.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Four Seismic Zones of India \(IS 1893:2016 Part 1\):) Tj
T*
(   India is categorized into four seismic zones, with corresponding Zone Factors \(Z, representing) Tj
T*
(   peak ground acceleration PGA as a fraction of gravity\):) Tj
T*
(   - Zone II \(Low Seismic Hazard, Z = 0.10\):) Tj
T*
(   * Geographic Coverage: Stable central and southern Deccan Plateau \(parts of Karnataka, Andhra) Tj
