(   3. Earthquake-Resistant Structural Engineering Principles:) Tj
T*
(   - Ductility and Confinement: Enforcing IS 13920 ductile detailing in reinforced concrete \(RC\)) Tj
T*
(   frames. Providing close stirrup spacing \(shear ties\) in beam-column junctions to prevent) Tj
T*
(   brittle shear failure.) Tj
T*
(   - Base Isolation Systems: Employs elastomeric lead-rubber bearings \(LRBs\) beneath building) Tj
T*
(   foundations to uncouple superstructure from horizontal ground vibrations.) Tj
T*
(   - Symmetrical Structural Configuration: Avoiding soft storeys \(open ground floor parking\) and) Tj
T*
(   structural torsional irregularities that amplify earthquake collapse.) Tj
