(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the geotechnical physics of Soil Liquefaction during earthquakes, cyclic shear stresses, and mitigation via vibro-compaction.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Geotechnical Mechanics of Soil Liquefaction and Ground Improvement Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Definition of Liquefaction:) Tj
T*
(   Soil liquefaction is a devastating geotechnical phenomenon wherein saturated, loose,) Tj
T*
(   cohesionless granular soils \(fine sands and silty sands\) temporarily lose their shear strength) Tj
T*
(   and stiffness during strong cyclic earthquake shaking, transforming from a solid state into a) Tj
T*
(   viscous liquid suspension.) Tj
T*
(   2. Geotechnical Mechanism and Effective Stress Principle:) Tj
T*
(   Governed by Karl Terzaghi's Principle of Effective Stress:) Tj
T*
(   sigma' = sigma_total - u) Tj
T*
(   Where sigma' is effective intergranular contact stress, sigma_total is total overburden stress,) Tj
T*
(   and u is pore water pressure.) Tj
T*
(   - Coulomb-Mohr Shear Strength Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   tau_f = c + sigma' * tan\(phi\)) Tj
T*
(   For cohesionless sands \(c = 0\): tau_f = \(sigma_total - u\) * tan\(phi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cyclic Seismic Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Loose sands naturally contract during shearing as sand grains attempt to densify into tighter) Tj
T*
(   packing.) Tj
T*
