(   3. Surface Manifestations and Structural Failures:) Tj
T*
(   - Sand Boils and Mud Volcanoes: High subterranean hydrostatic pressure forces liquefying sand) Tj
T*
(   slurries upward through ground fissures, erupting onto the surface.) Tj
T*
(   - Loss of Bearing Capacity: High-rise buildings tilt, rotate, or sink bodily into the liquefied) Tj
T*
(   ground without structural fracture \(e.g., Niigata earthquake, 1964\).) Tj
T*
(   - Lateral Spreading: Gentle coastal slopes liquefy and slide horizontally toward rivers or) Tj
T*
