(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the hydrodynamics of Tsunamis, the conservation of energy in the Shoaling Effect, and DART ocean bottom early warning systems.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Tsunami Hydrodynamics, Shoaling Amplification Mechanics, and DART Early Warning Networks:) Tj
T*
(   1. Hydrodynamic Genesis of Tsunamis:) Tj
T*
(   A tsunami is a series of catastrophic ocean gravity waves generated by a sudden, large-scale) Tj
T*
(   vertical displacement of the seafloor, most commonly caused by undersea thrust earthquakes at) Tj
T*
(   subduction zones \(e.g., 2004 Indian Ocean Tsunami, 2011 Tohoku Tsunami\), submarine volcanic) Tj
T*
(   collapses, or submarine landslides.) Tj
T*
(   2. Deep-Water Propagation Physics \(Shallow-Water Wave Theory\):) Tj
T*
(   - In physical oceanography, a wave is classified as a 'Shallow-Water Wave' when ocean water) Tj
T*
(   depth \(h\) is much smaller than its wavelength \(L\): h / L < 0.05.) Tj
T*
(   - Tsunamis possess immense wavelengths: L = 100 to 500 kilometers! Even in the deepest oceanic) Tj
T*
(   trenches \(h = 4 to 6 km\), h / L < 0.05. Therefore, tsunamis behave as shallow-water waves) Tj
T*
(   everywhere in the global ocean!) Tj
T*
(   - Tsunami Wave Velocity \(v\):) Tj
T*
(   v = sqrt\( g * h \)) Tj
T*
(   Where g is gravity \(9.81 m/s2\) and h is ocean depth.) Tj
T*
(   * At depth h = 4,000 meters: v = sqrt\(9.81 * 4000\) ~ 198 m/s ~ 713 km/h \(speed of a commercial) Tj
T*
(   passenger jet!\).) Tj
T*
(   * In deep water, the wave amplitude is very small \(H ~ 0.5 to 1.0 meter\) spread over hundreds) Tj
T*
(   of kilometers; ships at sea pass over tsunamis without noticing them.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Coastal Shoaling Amplification Effect \(Green's Law\):) Tj
T*
(   - By conservation of energy, the energy flux \(E_flux\) of the tsunami wave train moving toward) Tj
T*
(   land must remain constant \(neglecting minor friction\):) Tj
T*
(   E_flux = \(1/8\) * rho * g * H^2 * v = constant.) Tj
T*
(   Since v = sqrt\(g * h\): H^2 * sqrt\(h\) = constant => H proportional to h^\(-1/4\) \(Green's Law\).) Tj
T*
(   - As the tsunami enters shallow coastal waters:) Tj
T*
(   * Water depth h collapses from 4,000 m down to 10 m.) Tj
T*
(   * Wave velocity drops from 700 km/h down to 35 km/h.) Tj
T*
