(   1. Industrial Chemical Profile: Methyl Isocyanate \(MIC\):) Tj
T*
(   Methyl Isocyanate \(CH3-N=C=O, MW = 57.05 g/mol\) was synthesized at the Union Carbide India) Tj
T*
(   Limited \(UCIL\) Bhopal facility as a chemical intermediate in the manufacture of the carbamate) Tj
T*
(   pesticide Carbaryl \(Sevin\):) Tj
T*
(   - Synthesis: Methylamine reacts with Phosgene:) Tj
T*
(   CH3NH2 + COCl2 -> CH3NH-CO-Cl + HCl -> CH3-N=C=O \(MIC\) + 2 HCl) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Properties: Highly volatile liquid \(boiling point 39.1 deg C, vapor pressure 348) Tj
T*
(   mmHg at 20 deg C\). Extremely reactive, toxic, and lachrymatory.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Fatal Chemical Runaway in Storage Tank 610:) Tj
T*
(   On the night of December 2, 1984, approximately 500 to 1,000 kg of water accidentally entered) Tj
T*
(   underground stainless steel Storage Tank 610 during a routine filter line water-washing) Tj
T*
(   operation \(due to missing slip-blind isolation plates\):) Tj
T*
(   - Exothermic Water Hydrolysis:) Tj
T*
(   CH3-N=C=O + H2O -> [CH3-NH-COOH] \(Unstable methylcarbamic acid\)) Tj
T*
(   [CH3-NH-COOH] -> CH3NH2 \(Methylamine\) + CO2 \(g\) + Heat \(-84 kJ/mol\).) Tj
T*
(   - Autocatalytic Secondary Reactions:) Tj
T*
(   The generated methylamine reacted violently with remaining MIC:) Tj
T*
(   CH3NCO + CH3NH2 -> CH3-NH-CO-NH-CH3 \(1,3-Dimethylurea\) + Heat.) Tj
T*
(   - Catalytic Trimerization:) Tj
T*
(   Corrosion in the tank wall had released iron rust contaminants \(Fe3+\). In the presence of) Tj
T*
(   ferric catalysts and elevated temperatures, MIC underwent explosive trimerization:) Tj
T*
(   3 CH3NCO --[Fe3+, Heat]--> \(CH3NCO\)3 \(Trimethyl isocyanurate\) + Heat \(-134 kJ/mol\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thermal Runaway: Because heat generation far exceeded the tank's dissipation capacity,) Tj
T*
(   internal temperature surged above 200 deg C, and internal pressure skyrocketed to 55 psi \(3.8) Tj
T*
(   bar\), violently rupturing the tank safety relief valve.) Tj
T*
(   3. Catastrophic Multiple Safety System Failures:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Tank Refrigeration System: Designed to keep MIC stored at 0 deg C to suppress runaway) Tj
T*
(   reactions; had been decommissioned months earlier to save electricity costs!) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Vent Gas Scrubber: Designed to neutralize venting gases with 10% caustic soda \(NaOH\); was) Tj
T*
(   unpowered and out of service.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Flare Tower: Designed to combust leaking toxic gases; disconnected for maintenance.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Water Curtain Sprayers: Water pressure was insufficient to reach the elevated gas) Tj
T*
(   discharge stack!) Tj
T*
(   - Consequence: Over 40 metric tons of lethal MIC and breakdown products \(HCN, phosgene\) vented) Tj
T*
(   into the cool night air, drifting over densely populated informal settlements, causing) Tj
T*
(   immediate death of over 3,800 people and chronic disability in over 500,000 survivors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 25:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the long-term clinical toxicology, pulmonary pathophysiology, and genetic teratogenicity in survivors of the Bhopal Gas Disaster.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Clinical Toxicology, Pulmonary Pathophysiology, and Chronic Aftermath of Bhopal:) Tj
T*
(   1. Acute Inhalation Toxicology:) Tj
T*
(   Inhaled Methyl Isocyanate vapor contacts moist mucosal membranes of the respiratory tract and) Tj
T*
(   eyes:) Tj
T*
(   - Ocular Pathology: Severe chemical keratitis, corneal edema, corneal ulceration, and permanent) Tj
T*
(   blindness.) Tj
T*
(   - Upper Airway Destruction: Necrosis and sloughing of tracheobronchial epithelium, causing) Tj
T*
(   acute laryngeal spasms and asphyxiation.) Tj
T*
(   - Alveolar-Capillary Membrane Rupture: Hydrolysis produces methylamine and cyanate ions that) Tj
T*
(   cross the alveolar epithelium, destroying capillary endothelial junctions. Massive) Tj
T*
(   intra-alveolar hemorrhage and pulmonary edema followed, with victims essentially 'drowning in) Tj
T*
(   their own body fluids.') Tj
T*
