(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the institutional architecture and statutory mandates under the Disaster Management Act, 2005: NDMA, SDMA, and DDMA.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Indian Disaster Management Act, 2005: Institutional Architecture and Statutory Mandates:) Tj
T*
(   1. Legislative Mandate and Institutional Transition:) Tj
T*
(   Enacted in December 2005 following the traumatic lessons of the 1999 Odisha Super Cyclone, 2001) Tj
T*
(   Bhuj Earthquake, and 2004 Indian Ocean Tsunami. The Act marked a paradigm shift from a) Tj
T*
(   post-disaster reactive relief approach to a holistic, proactive, multi-hazard disaster risk) Tj
T*
(   reduction framework.) Tj
T*
(   2. Three-Tier Institutional Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. National Level: National Disaster Management Authority \(NDMA\):) Tj
T*
(   * Apex statutory policy-making body, headed ex-officio by the Prime Minister of India.) Tj
T*
(   * Formulates national disaster policies, approves the National Disaster Management Plan, and) Tj
T*
(   issues binding guidelines to ministries and state authorities.) Tj
T*
(   * National Executive Committee \(NEC\): Headed by the Union Home Secretary, assists NDMA and) Tj
T*
(   coordinates inter-ministerial operational deployment.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. State Level: State Disaster Management Authority \(SDMA\):) Tj
T*
(   * Headed ex-officio by the Chief Minister of the State.) Tj
T*
(   * Approves State Disaster Management Plans, coordinates resource mobilization, and oversees) Tj
T*
(   state departmental disaster response.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. District Level: District Disaster Management Authority \(DDMA\):) Tj
T*
(   * The frontline operational engine of disaster management in India.) Tj
T*
(   * Headed by the District Magistrate \(Collector / Deputy Commissioner\) as Chairperson, with the) Tj
T*
(   elected Chairperson of the Zilla Parishad as Co-Chairperson.) Tj
T*
(   * Prepares district disaster management plans, coordinates local police, fire, health, and) Tj
T*
(   NGOs, and orders emergency evacuations.) Tj
T*
(   3. Dedicated Response and Financial Institutions:) Tj
T*
(   - National Disaster Response Force \(NDRF\): Specialized multi-disciplinary paramilitary force) Tj
T*
(   trained in chemical, biological, radiological, and nuclear \(CBRN\) emergencies and) Tj
T*
(   search-and-rescue.) Tj
T*
(   - National Institute of Disaster Management \(NIDM\): Mandated for specialized capacity building,) Tj
T*
(   training, and research.) Tj
T*
ET

