(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the Disaster Management Cycle, detailing the sequential activities across Mitigation, Preparedness, Emergency Response, and Recovery.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Disaster Management Cycle: Operational Phases and Resilience Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circular Operational Framework:) Tj
T*
(   The Disaster Management Cycle illustrates the ongoing process through which governments, civil) Tj
T*
(   society, and businesses plan for and reduce the impact of disasters, react during and) Tj
T*
(   immediately following a crisis, and recover afterward:) Tj
T*
(   2. Pre-Disaster Risk Reduction Phase \(Before Hazard Event\):) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Mitigation:) Tj
T*
(   * Long-term structural and non-structural measures taken to eliminate or permanently reduce the) Tj
T*
(   baseline risk of hazards:) Tj
T*
(   * Structural: Retrofitting vulnerable buildings with seismic dampers, constructing coastal) Tj
T*
(   cyclone storm surge shelters, building concrete sea walls, constructing flood retention) Tj
T*
(   reservoirs, and river dredging.) Tj
T*
(   * Non-Structural: Enforcing land-use zoning bylaws \(prohibiting construction in active) Tj
T*
(   floodplains or liquefiable soil zones\), enforcing stringent building codes, and preserving) Tj
T*
(   coastal mangrove buffers.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Preparedness:) Tj
T*
(   * Developing actionable readiness plans before an event strikes:) Tj
T*
(   * Establishing multi-hazard satellite and radar Early Warning Systems \(EWS\), preparing) Tj
T*
(   community evacuation routes, conducting regular mock drills, stockpiling emergency food,) Tj
T*
(   medicine, and water reserves, and training community first responders.) Tj
T*
(   3. Post-Disaster Emergency Phase \(During and Immediately After Event\):) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Emergency Response:) Tj
T*
(   * Life-saving actions executed in the golden hours: Search and rescue operations \(NDRF) Tj
T*
(   deployment\), emergency medical triage, mass evacuation, establishing temporary relief camps,) Tj
T*
(   and providing clean drinking water to prevent cholera epidemics.) Tj
T*
(   4. Post-Disaster Restoration Phase \(After Hazard Event\):) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Recovery and Rehabilitation:) Tj
T*
(   * Short-term: Restoring critical lifelines \(electricity grid, potable water mains,) Tj
T*
(   telecommunication towers, transport bridges\).) Tj
T*
(   * Long-term: Reconstruction of permanent resilient housing, psychological counseling for trauma) Tj
T*
(   survivors, and restoring economic livelihoods.) Tj
T*
(   - The 'Build Back Better' Paradigm: Ensuring reconstructed infrastructure possesses superior) Tj
T*
(   structural resilience than pre-disaster assets to resist future hazard events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
