12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the four priority areas and seven global targets of the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction \(2015-2030\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction \(2015-2030\): Priorities and Global Targets:) Tj
T*
(   1. International Mandate and Adoption:) Tj
T*
(   Adopted at the Third UN World Conference on Disaster Risk Reduction in Sendai, Miyagi, Japan,) Tj
T*
(   in March 2015, the Sendai Framework is a 15-year, voluntary, non-binding agreement that) Tj
T*
(   succeeded the Hyogo Framework for Action \(HFA 2005-2015\).) Tj
T*
(   - Core Expected Outcome: 'The substantial reduction of disaster risk and losses in lives,) Tj
T*
(   livelihoods and health and in the economic, physical, social, cultural and environmental assets) Tj
T*
