T*
(   2. The Four Priority Action Areas:) Tj
T*
(   - Priority 1: Understanding Disaster Risk:) Tj
T*
(   Promoting the collection, analysis, and dissemination of disaggregated disaster data; mapping) Tj
T*
(   multi-hazard geospatial vulnerabilities and climate risk modeling.) Tj
T*
(   - Priority 2: Strengthening Disaster Risk Governance to Manage Disaster Risk:) Tj
T*
(   Enacting robust legislative frameworks, empowering decentralized local authorities, and) Tj
T*
(   fostering multi-sectoral public-private coordination.) Tj
T*
(   - Priority 3: Investing in Disaster Risk Reduction for Resilience:) Tj
T*
(   Allocating dedicated public capital and mobilizing private investment into structural) Tj
T*
(   resilience, retrofitting critical infrastructure \(schools, hospitals\), and nature-based) Tj
T*
(   solutions.) Tj
T*
(   - Priority 4: Enhancing Disaster Preparedness for Effective Response and to 'Build Back Better') Tj
T*
(   in Recovery, Rehabilitation, and Reconstruction:) Tj
T*
(   Equipping emergency responders, conducting international mutual-aid training, and utilizing) Tj
T*
(   post-disaster recovery to upgrade infrastructure resilience.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Seven Global Targets \(A to G\):) Tj
T*
(   - Target A: Substantially reduce global disaster mortality by 2030.) Tj
T*
(   - Target B: Substantially reduce the number of affected people globally by 2030.) Tj
T*
(   - Target C: Reduce direct disaster economic loss in relation to global Gross Domestic Product) Tj
T*
(   \(GDP\).) Tj
T*
(   - Target D: Substantially reduce disaster damage to critical infrastructure and disruption of) Tj
T*
(   basic services \(health and educational facilities\).) Tj
T*
(   - Target E: Substantially increase the number of countries with national and local disaster) Tj
T*
(   risk reduction strategies.) Tj
T*
(   - Target F: Substantially enhance international cooperation to developing countries.) Tj
T*
(   - Target G: Substantially increase the availability of and access to multi-hazard early warning) Tj
T*
(   systems \(MHEWS\) and disaster risk information.) Tj
