/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Differentiate the four typologies of Drought \(Meteorological, Hydrological, Agricultural, Socioeconomic\), and describe drought mitigation engineering.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Typologies of Drought, Propagation Mechanisms, and Mitigation Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Progressive Cascade of Drought:) Tj
T*
(   Drought is an insidious natural hazard characterized by a deficiency of precipitation over an) Tj
T*
(   extended period, resulting in a water shortage that causes adverse impacts on vegetation,) Tj
T*
(   agriculture, and human populations:) Tj
T*
(   2. The Four Sequential Drought Typologies:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Meteorological Drought:) Tj
T*
(   * Defined purely on the basis of physical rainfall deficit relative to long-term climatological) Tj
T*
(   normal precipitation over a region \(e.g., IMD classifies rainfall deficit of 26-50% as Moderate) Tj
T*
(   Drought, and > 50% as Severe Drought\).) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Hydrological Drought:) Tj
T*
(   * Occurs when meteorological drought persists, leading to marked depletion of surface water) Tj
T*
(   bodies \(drying up of streams, rivers, lakes, and storage reservoirs\) and steep declines in) Tj
T*
(   regional groundwater table levels.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Agricultural Drought:) Tj
T*
(   * Occurs when soil moisture in the plant root zone drops below the Permanent Wilting Point) Tj
T*
(   \(PWP\) during critical crop phenological growth stages, causing vegetative wilting, stunted) Tj
T*
(   biomass, and massive crop yield failure.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Socioeconomic Drought:) Tj
T*
(   * Occurs when physical water shortages begin to disrupt the economic supply and demand of) Tj
T*
