BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Quantitative Risk Assessment \(QRA\) for Major Accident Hazard \(MAH\) industrial chemical facilities: HAZOP and Fault Tree Analysis \(FTA\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Quantitative Risk Assessment \(QRA\), HAZOP Methodology, and Fault Tree Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Legislative Mandate for Chemical Safety:) Tj
T*
(   In India, Major Accident Hazard \(MAH\) industrial facilities handling hazardous chemicals are) Tj
T*
(   strictly regulated under the Manufacture, Storage and Import of Hazardous Chemical \(MSIHC\)) Tj
T*
(   Rules, 1989, and the Chemical Accidents \(Emergency Planning, Preparedness, and Response\) Rules,) Tj
T*
(   1996, enacted under EPA 1986. Operators must conduct formal Quantitative Risk Assessments) Tj
T*
(   \(QRA\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Hazard and Operability \(HAZOP\) Study Methodology:) Tj
T*
(   - Systematic Qualitative Technique: A structured, multidisciplinary team review designed to) Tj
T*
(   identify operational deviations in process flowsheets that could lead to catastrophic accidents) Tj
T*
(   or production losses.) Tj
T*
(   - Guide Word Approach: Standard guide words \(NO / NONE, MORE, LESS, AS WELL AS, PART OF,) Tj
T*
(   REVERSE, OTHER THAN\) are systematically applied to process parameters \(Flow, Pressure,) Tj
T*
(   Temperature, Level, Viscosity\) at every process 'Node':) Tj
T*
(   * Node: Reactor cooling jacket line.) Tj
T*
(   * Parameter: Flow.) Tj
T*
(   * Guide Word: NO.) Tj
T*
(   * Deviation: 'NO FLOW' of cooling water.) Tj
T*
(   * Cause: Cooling water circulation pump electrical trip.) Tj
T*
(   * Consequence: Exothermic heat accumulation, thermal runaway reaction, reactor) Tj
T*
(   over-pressurization, and explosive rupture.) Tj
T*
(   * Engineering Safeguards: High-temperature interlock sensor triggering automated emergency) Tj
T*
(   backup cooling water pump, and rupture disc ducted to an engineered dump tank.) Tj
T*
(   3. Fault Tree Analysis \(FTA\) Quantitative Modeling:) Tj
T*
(   - Deductive Logic Architecture: Top-down logic diagram that begins with an unwanted) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic Top Event \(e.g., 'Catastrophic Toxic Gas Release from Storage Vessel'\) and works) Tj
T*
(   backward to deduce all possible combinations of basic hardware failures, human errors, and) Tj
T*
(   environmental events capable of causing the top event.) Tj
T*
(   - Boolean Logic Gates:) Tj
T*
(   * AND Gate: The output event occurs if and only if ALL input events occur simultaneously:) Tj
T*
(   P_out = P_1 * P_2 * ... * P_n \(Redundant independent safety barriers\).) Tj
T*
(   * OR Gate: The output event occurs if ANY ONE of the input events occurs:) Tj
T*
(   P_out = 1 - [ \(1 - P_1\) * \(1 - P_2\) * ... * \(1 - P_n\) ] ~ P_1 + P_2 + ... + P_n \(Single points) Tj
T*
(   of failure\).) Tj
T*
(   - Calculation of Top Event Frequency: Multiplying component failure rates along cut sets to) Tj
T*
(   quantify overall failure probability per operational year, ensuring risk falls within As Low As) Tj
T*
(   Reasonably Practicable \(ALARP\) safety criteria.) Tj
T*
ET

